        'Compounding cumulative blindness is a structural conflict of interest at the heart of Indian EIA practice: the accredited environmental consultant who collects baseline data and authors the impact report is selected and paid directly by the project proponent seeking clearance. Until scientific baseline certification is severed financially from proponent patronage, academic integrity at Hazratbal will remain systematically sidelined by commercial consultancy paperwork at the clearance table.',
