        'Financially, SEGP-WH requires no unrealistic treasury windfall: dedicating a statutory 1.5 percent telemetry-and-verification earmark from capital lake-conservation, Smart City, and highway DPR budgets, pooled with Polluter-Pays Environmental Compensation escrows, fully funds continuous NABL-grade university–regulator joint laboratories and an independent Proponent-Blind EIA Escrow Fund. Success is judged solely by measurable five-year physical outcomes—winter 24-hour PM2.5 and black-carbon mass reductions, sustained dissolved oxygen above 6 mg/L across urban Jhelum/wetland outflows, zero net loss of Ramsar open-water bathymetry, and declining heavy-metal burdens in harvested aquatic foods.',
